**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitFitRunFileTests`

**How to implement.** A fit run persists as its own kit file, `<study>@<stamp>.fitrun-json`, in canonical JSON validated against its own schema, written once and never rewritten (001 §E 'Fit runs are append-only'; 001 §A; 001 §P '`KitProxy` … studies and fit runs'; the S11.3 brief 'Fit runs are append-only and never rewritten'; .spec-md §4 'Stored formats'). It reuses step 146's stack (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`) and step 359's shape for studies; no second parser or writer is written, and no proxy verb is added: append-only is a check over `listKindFiles` before `writeKindFile` (step 127). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. (1) `Kit.fs`: `KitError` (step 122) gains `FitRunExistsErr of reason : string` (the kit already holds a fit run of that name), rendered `the kit already holds that fit run: <reason>`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/fitrun.schema.json`, draft 2020-12 like `schema/study.schema.json` (step 359), `$id` `https://berreman/schema/fitrun.json`: `schemaVersion` a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 (`then`), the root holds exactly the fifteen fields of `FitRun` (step 383): `name` and `study` (strings holding a non-white-space character, `\S`), `stamp` (a string), `mode` (an integer from 1 to 2), `stage` (1 to 3), `calibrationUse` (1 to 2), `engine` (1 to 2), `runs` (an array of non-empty strings), `dataRead`, `parameters`, `entries`, `members` and `objectMatrices` (arrays) and `notes` (a string). The inner shapes are bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one. It is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest` beside `schema/study.schema.json` in `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no comment. `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `validateFitRunFile (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` over `validateWith`, its schema loaded once behind a `lazy` that loads the common schema first, as `validateStudyFile` (step 359) does. (3) `CanonicalJson.options` (`CanonicalJson.fs`) gains three converters, for `FitStage`, `CalibrationUse` and `StudyEngineKind`, written as step 359's `ParameterScope` and `FitMode` converters are and registered beside them: each writes the case's `value` and reads through `tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. `FitMemberOutcome` and `UnknownOwner` keep the serializer's case form; nothing else in the options changes. (4) `KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146, 359): `type FitRun with member this.fileText : Result<KitFileText, StorageError>` (`nodeOf this` rendered by `canonicalFileText`); `type KitFileText with member this.parseFitRun : Result<FitRun, StorageError>` (`parseVersionedText validateFitRunFile FitRunKitFile.extension FitRun.currentSchemaVersion this.value`); on the `KitProxy` extension `member this.writeFitRun (run : FitRun) : Result<unit, KitError>`: when `listKindFiles FitRunKitFile` holds `run.name.fileStem` (step 383) ignoring case, `FitRunExistsErr` naming the file, writing nothing; otherwise `writeKindFile FitRunKitFile run.name.fileStem` of `run.fileText`, a rendering error being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file; and `member this.readFitRuns (study : StudyName) : Result<FitRun list, KitError>`, which parses every stem `listKindFiles FitRunKitFile` answers, a refusal or a run whose `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason and refusing the whole read, and answers the runs whose `study` is the given one, ordered by `stamp` then by name (ordinal). Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) `writeFitRun` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. No delete, rename, replace, cache or other member is added: a fit run is written once. Tests. Their fit run is test-local: `QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z` of study `QZ-LR` at that instant, `JointFit`, `ObjectStage`, `CalibrationHeldFixed`, `LinearStudyEngine`, runs [E1], one `DataAttachment` (`data/raw/e1.csv`, a test-local hash), one `FitRunParameter` (CPL1 `c2.retardance`, a `CalibratedParameter`), one `FitRunEntry` (QZ `m00`, its `ItemOwner`, start 1, fitted 0.98), one member (start [1], `MemberConverged ([0.98], Some (FitChiSquared 0.5))`), one `ObjectMatrixFit` (QZ, sixteen elements, rank 16, RMSE 0.01) and two lines of notes. `KitContentFileJsonTests`: `a fit run is stored under its name`: `FitRunKitFile.fileNameOf` of its name's `fileStem` is `FileName "QZ-LR@20261101T120000Z.fitrun-json"`; `a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text`: `fileText` then `parseFitRun` answers an equal run; the text holds no `\r`, ends with exactly one `\n`, lists its top-level keys in ordinal order, writes the mode, stage, calibration use and engine as their tags, and writing the parsed run again gives the same text; `a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused`: the text with `schemaVersion` 2 answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` (found 2, expected 1, `fileExtension = FitRunKitFile.extension`), without `entries`, with an extra top-level key or with `stage` 4 `SchemaValidationErr`, and `{` `MalformedJsonErr`. `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 359): `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes each `FitStage`, `CalibrationUse` and `StudyEngineKind` as its tag and reads it back, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the stage tag 4, the use tag 3 and the engine tag 3. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitFitRunFileTests.fs`, `module KitFitRunFileTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, whose facts each make a folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "KitFitRunFileTests", <a new GUID>)` and a `KitProxy.create` over it with `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file (step 359's precedent): `a kit's fit runs round-trip, each under its name, read per study in stamp order`: the run above, a second of `QZ-LR` an hour later and one of study `LR` written answer three `.fitrun-json` files named by their stems, `readFitRuns (StudyName "QZ-LR")` the two in stamp order and `readFitRuns (StudyName "LR")` the one; `a fit run is never rewritten: writing its name again is FitRunExistsErr and leaves the file's bytes`: writing the run again, and a run of the same name with other entries, each answer `FitRunExistsErr` naming the file, and the file's bytes are unchanged; `a read-only kit refuses a fit run write and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView` `writeFitRun` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and the folder's bytes are unchanged. `KitTests`' `every kit error renders its condition and its payload` covers the new case.

**Acceptance.** After the fit-run file lands, `KitProxy.writeFitRun` MUST write a fit run once as `<name>.fitrun-json` in canonical JSON and refuse an existing name with `FitRunExistsErr`, writing nothing, and `readFitRuns` MUST read a study's runs in stamp order; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a fit run is stored under its name`, `a fit run file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a fit run file of another schema version, a schema-invalid one or a malformed one is refused`, `a kit's fit runs round-trip, each under its name, read per study in stamp order`, `a fit run is never rewritten: writing its name again is FitRunExistsErr and leaves the file's bytes` and `a read-only kit refuses a fit run write and writes nothing`, the count rising by 6, and the widened `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back`, `an unknown disk tag is refused` and `every kit error renders its condition and its payload`; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.
